From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:26:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: BTW beside Steer asks a queued message on the side
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.45 (ask 69, 2026-11-16). 0115 answers a composer
message that starts with /btw at once, in a card; 0116 gave each queued
message a Steer. A message already queued behind a running turn had no way
to become a side question short of retyping it. Each queued row now has a
BTW button, offered when the agent takes side questions: the message
leaves the queue and is asked through 0115's path, answered in its card
and kept out of the conversation. A message already written as `/btw ...`
is read as the composer reads it.

A side question is text only, so a queued message carrying a mention or an
image keeps BTW disabled, with the reason in its tooltip. 0115's card
building moved into ThreadView::show_side_question so both paths share it.
Tests in thread_view/queue_side_question_tests.rs; Red seen with a
non-text block accepted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
